-527dc7e0482e" :question/math-academy-id "q-116082" :question/problem "What is the center of the hyperbola $\\frac{(x+2)^{2}}{5}-\\frac{(y-4)^{2}}{6}=1?$" :question/worked-solution "The equation of a horizontal hyperbola centered at $(h,k)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nNote that the given equation can be rewritten as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-(-2))^{2}}{(\\sqrt{5})^{2}}-\\frac{(y-4)^{2}}{(\\sqrt{6})^{2}}=1\n$$\n\nIn this case, $h=-2$ and $k=4.$\n\nTherefore, the center of the hyperbola is $(-2,4).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-116082/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f99d4fec-bc58-5a09-9fac-38b46f233489"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-116082"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-328251/field-1/4de395131b8c6206950603752bf3404c42f4dd6f0a41fee38e42388d1b92c133" :answer/id #uuid "0c39c2cc-56f3-5642-945c-087f873dbbaf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-328251/field-1/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" :answer/id #uuid "c70d9036-7ad0-53ec-9ae2-f33ad6fe6619" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-328251/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "d7bf8169-1425-584e-910d-78a3a2cf7911" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-328251/field-1/4de395131b8c6206950603752bf3404c42f4dd6f0a41fee38e42388d1b92c133" :answer-field/choices ["q-328251/field-1/4de395131b8c6206950603752bf3404c42f4dd6f0a41fee38e42388d1b92c133" "q-328251/field-1/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-328251/field-2/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "5ae9e204-3813-5fdd-8c18-78ba635df7a2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensur