"q-328296/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cdab0134-e416-51cf-89fa-73ad4a2c2eb9"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-328296"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-16381"] :question/worked-solution "The equation of a horizontal hyperbola centered at $(h,k)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nTo rewrite the equation of the hyperbola in standard form, we need to group $x$ and $y$ terms and complete the squares as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6{x}^{2}-5{y}^{2}+72x+70y & =59 \\\\ 6{x}^{2}+72x-5{y}^{2}+70y & =59 \\\\ 6[{x}^{2}+12x]-5[{y}^{2}-14y] & =59 \\\\ 6((x+6)^{2}-36)-5[(y-7)^{2}-49] & =59 \\\\ 6(x+6)^{2}-216-5(y-7)^{2}+245 & =59 \\\\ 6(x+6)^{2}-5(y-7)^{2} & =59+216-245 \\\\ 6(x+6)^{2}-5(y-7)^{2} & =30 \\\\ \\frac{(x+6)^{2}}{5}-\\frac{(y-7)^{2}}{6} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the center is $(-6,7).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-328439/field-1/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "7b883e4f-40f4-5477-a59c-507110d58207" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-328439/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "fe779c7f-2523-50c7-93c9-2b04be90f886" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-328439/field-1/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer-field/choices ["q-328439/field-1/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-328439/field-2/b13ac151352392d38026eed875b911708c50c896d6c09463410ac041030163ff" :answer/id #uuid "c1fc9138-91d5-59c6-9dc3-708b62ae9036" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-328439/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "f3f3a879-6370-5c22-a604-b08081154ad1" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-328439/field-2/b13ac151352392d38026eed875b911708c50c896d6c09463410ac041030163ff" :answer-field/choices ["q-328439/field-2/b13ac151352392d38026eed875b911708c50c896d6c09463410ac041030163ff"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-328439" :question/id #uuid "aa53e21b-f9a9-54c9-a82e-86616efd16dc" :question/math-academy-id "q-328439" :question/problem "The center of the hyperbola $16{x}^{2}-9{y}^{2}-54y=-63$ is$\\,\\,($\n{{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}}\n$).$" :question/worked-solution "The equation of a horizontal hyperbola centered at $(h,k)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nTo rewrite the equation of the hyperbola in standard form, we need to group $x$ and $y$ terms and complete the squares as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}16{x}^{2}-9{y}^{2}-54y & =-63 \\\\ 16{x}^{2}-[\\,9{y}^{2}+54y\\,] & =-63 \\\\ 16{x}^{2}-[\\,9({y}^{2}+6y)\\,] & =-63 \\\\ 16{x}^{2}-[\\,9((y+3)^{2}-9)\\,] & =-63 \\\\ 16{x}^{2}-9(y+3)^{2}+81 & =-63 \\\\ 16{x}^{2}-9(y+3)^{2} & =-63-81 \\\\ 16{x}^{2}-9(y+3)^{2} & =-144 \\\\ \\frac{(y+3)^{2}}{{4}^{2}}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{3}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(y-(-3))^{2}}{{4}^{2}}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{3}^{2}} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the center of the hyperbola is $(\\,0,-3\\,).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-328439/field-1" "q-328439/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "223e29c9-1bb5-51ee-9ec8-4d5c15363951"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-328439"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-78871/selection/64b40412b8b548e9db61b40e65e429295db220ca3aa45212f2011c9fabbd9c4b" :answer/id #uuid "246abdb3-c14e-5df5-b45b-4d68be2c2b14" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(-5,1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-78871/selection/8fbef25e0013385c5c4de2827f3f6377bb56f3bc145afd16f5385c69df073111" :answer/id #uuid "2801