\n\n$$\n\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nTo rewrite the equation of the hyperbola in the above form, we need to group $x$ and $y$ terms and complete the squares, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-3{x}^{2}+2{y}^{2}+12x-12y & =12 \\\\ 2{y}^{2}-12y-3{x}^{2}+12x & =12 \\\\ 2[{y}^{2}-6y]-3[{x}^{2}-4x] & =12 \\\\ 2[(y-3)^{2}-9]-3[(x-2)^{2}-4] & =12 \\\\ 2(y-3)^{2}-18-3(x-2)^{2}+12 & =12 \\\\ 2(y-3)^{2}-3(x-2)^{2} & =12+18-12 \\\\ 2(y-3)^{2}-3(x-2)^{2} & =18 \\\\ \\frac{(y-3)^{2}}{9}-\\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{6} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the center is $(2,3).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-78379/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "345d6df7-2ada-5c2e-8146-7c779afae3af"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-78379"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-10419/selection/f1c72963f33c0862d48b8a0d3db37a9a15f0086f42a830087c9caa8a9b6c8a48" :answer/id #uuid "07d77eb6-3fad-5839-93b1-2c0e93a78163" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(2,-2)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-10419/selection/020afe65abcbd214ce790da9b908e21b333d6a24716bc482d003e5b59a07e1cd" :answer/id #uuid "e9060fa3-2fe0-57a2-95c1-50128575180a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(2,2)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-10419/selection/ca6af7ae67072899bb0fa54a714cd69fb79e694a5b3fb02e9c2249473dfce856" :answer/id #uuid "fdf19b65-8c59-5ef3-b104-9ef16cdfbf7b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(4,2)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-10419/selection/e8b6e48d2640b190477b067d73ed38c8ae23d6a2118701d65bc1f8aac439d661" :answer/id #uuid "3ed0628e-5cbd-556f-b4c1-aa8f81743d20" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(-2,2)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-10419/selection/3daf7c7813fd10d96af0e7397ad761fd8013a7868d9b6c8ad4b2e20ce2d33dca" :answer/id #uuid "7b632a05-16eb-5468-962a-55d83edd788c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(2,4)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-10419/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "3abf1bc2-758a-57fb-a501-411d6468b38c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-10419/selection/020afe65abcbd214ce790da9b908e21b333d6a24716bc482d003e5b59a07e1cd" :answer-field/choices ["q-10419/selection/f1c72963f33c0862d48b8a0d3db37a9a15f0086f42a830087c9caa8a9b6c8a48" "q-10419/selection/020afe65abcbd214ce790da9b908e21b333d6a24716bc482d003e5b59a07e1cd" "q-10419/selection/ca6af7ae67072899bb0fa54a714cd69fb79e694a5b3fb02e9c2249473dfce856" "q-10419/selection/e8b6e48d2640b190477b067d73ed38c8ae23d6a2118701d65bc1f8aac439d661" "q-10419/selection/3daf7c7813fd10d96af0e7397ad761fd8013a7868d9b6c8ad4b2e20ce2d33dca"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-10419" :question/id #uuid "70a4a2a9-00d7-57b7-8107-169920caa030" :question/math-academy-id "q-10419" :question/problem "What is the center of the hyperbola $4{y}^{2}-{x}^{2}-16y+4x=0?$" :question/worked-solution "The equation of a vertical hyperbola centered at $(h,k)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nTo rewrite the equation of the hyperbola in the above form, we need to group $x$ and $y$ terms and complete the squares, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{y}^{2}-{x}^{2}-16y+4x & =0 \\\\ 4{y}^{2}-16y-{x}^{2}+4x & =0 \\\\ 4[{y}^{2}-4y]-[{x}^{2}-4x] & =0 \\\\ 4[(y-2)^{2}-4]-[(x-2)^{2}-4] & =0 \\\\ 4(y-2)^{2}-16-(x-2)^{2}+4 & =0 \\\\ 4(y-2)^{2}-(x-2)^{2} & =16-4 \\\\ 4(y-2)^{2}-(x-2)^{2} & =12 \\\\ \\frac{(y-2)^{2}}{3}-\\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{12} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the center is $(2,2).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-10419/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "345d6df7-2ada-5c2e-8146-7c779afae3af"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-10419"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
